  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A tapered tube of cemented sulphide crust, a metre and a half long, driven into a fissure to draw hot flow across a household&#39;s mats and fitted with a crust wedge that can be worked in to throttle it. Tubes are cut by the cutters, cemented by the tiers and set by whoever holds the fissure, so a single object passes through two of the three corporations before it is used. This one was pulled in 2281 when the household moved and is scaled inside to about half its bore. The wedge is missing, as it usually is.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
